  "step_1": "The decision reason can be applied to the decision problem. The reason requires calculating the sum of all outcomes for each lottery, independent of their probabilities. For Lottery A: 2500 + 2400 + 0 = 4900 Euros. For Lottery B: 2400 (repeated once, as it has only one outcome) = 2400 Euros. The reason would prefer Lottery A because 4900 > 2400. The relevant information (outcomes of each lottery) is fully available, so the reason can be applied.",
